    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc1044400001">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 7A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS APPOINT THE MEMBERS OF THE GOVERNING BODY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PRIOR TO FILING, DRAFTS OF THE 990 ARE SHARED WITH THE CEO, COO, AND THE FINANCE COMMITTEE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE CHAMBER'S MANAGEMENT COUNCIL RESPONSIBLE FOR MONITORING THE ORGANIZATION'S WRITTEN CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY. CONTRACTS AND/OR TRANSACTIONS THAT COULD GIVE RISE TO A CONFLICT OF INTEREST ARE REPORTED TO THE MANAGEMENT COUNCIL BY THE CHAMBER'S SENIOR MANAGEMENT. IF THERE IS A POTENTIAL CONFLICT, THE "POTENTIAL PARTY IN INTEREST" IS REMOVED FROM THE DELIBERATIONS AND THE MANAGEMENT COUNCIL MAKES A DECISION ON THE POTENTIAL TRANSACTION BASED ON ITS MERITS. OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, AND KEY EMPLOYEES ARE REQUIRED TO DISCLOSE INTERESTS THAT COULD GIVE RISE TO CONFLICTS. CHAMBER SENIOR MANAGEMENT DOES BRING POTENTIAL FINANCIAL CONFLICTS OF INTEREST TO THE MANAGEMENT COUNCIL PRIOR TO ANY DECISIONS BEING MADE, AND ANY INDIVIDUALS WITH CONFLICTS ARE REQUIRED TO WITHDRAW FROM VOTING ON THE MATTER. WITH RESPECT TO PUBLIC POLICY ISSUES, OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, AND COMMITTEE MEMBERS ARE ASKED IF THEY MIGHT BE A PARTY IN INTEREST TO A PARTICULAR PUBLIC POLICY MATTER WHICH MIGHT COME BEFORE THE CHAMBER'S BOARD AND FOR WHICH THE CHAMBER MAY TAKE A POSITION. THESE INDIVIDUALS, IF THEY ARE "CONFLICTED", ARE ASKED TO DISCLOSE THE POTENTIAL CONFLICT AND WITHDRAW FROM VOTING ON THE MATTER.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE FORM 990, FORM 1023, AND GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, SUCH AS CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY, ARE AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART IX, LINE 11G</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PROFESSIONAL FEES: PROGRAM SERVICE EXPENSES 3,374. MANAGEMENT AND GENERAL EXPENSES 0. FUNDRAISING EXPENSES 0. TOTAL EXPENSES 3,374.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART XII, LINE 2C:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION'S PROCESSES FOR OVERSIGHT OF THE AUDIT OF ITS FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AND SELECTION OF AN INDEPENDENT ACCOUNTANT HAVE NOT CHANGED FROM PREVIOUS YEAR.</ExplanationTxt>
